    <briefdescription>
<para>Functions for the description of transversely isotropic elastic behavior. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Poisson&apos;s ratio <formula id="23">$\nu_{ij}$</formula> is defined as the negative ratio of the lateral strain in direction <formula id="24">$x_j$</formula> to the axial strain in direction <formula id="25">$x_i$</formula> for uniaxial stress applied in direction <formula id="25">$x_i$</formula>,</para>
<para><formula id="26">\[  \displaystyle \nu_{ij} = -\frac{\varepsilon_j}{\varepsilon_i}
  \quad\text{for}\quad \sigma_i \neq 0,\ \sigma_k = 0\ (k \neq i),
\]</formula></para>
<para>so the corresponding compliance entry reads <formula id="27">$ \mathbb{C}^{-1}_{ji} = -\nu_{ij}/E_i $</formula>. Symmetry of the compliance tensor implies <formula id="28">$ \nu_{ij}/E_i = \nu_{ji}/E_j $</formula>, hence only <formula id="29">$\nu_{12}$</formula> and <formula id="30">$\nu_{23}$</formula> are independent. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
